./services/platform/backend/MIGRATION.md:121:| conversations         | done                               | inc 51 (Tier A): migration 0036 (`app.conversations` + `app.conversation_messages` — messages carry a monotonic `seq` and an expression index on the sentAt→deliveredAt→createdAt chronology, the shared `message-order` contract REUSED for both the walk and the monotonic `lastMessageAt` advance) + `domains/conversations/service.ts`: the assignment-privacy predicate REUSED verbatim (`conversation_assignment.ts` — unassigned rows are ADMIN-TRIAGE ONLY, fail-closed; list scope filters post-page exactly like the 0.4 RLS), ingest-side create + message append (delivery-state defaults by direction, inbound bumps `metadata.unread_count`, never-stamped rows HEALED with the first connector name), keyset Inbox listing with batched contact + last-message joins (no N+1), status/unread counters, admin-gated assignment (individual + team-queue with org validation) wired to NEW collab emitters (`notifyConversationAssigned`/`…Team` — self-assign silent, team fan-out actor-excluded and bounded at 500), bulk verbs folded onto one core (same target statuses + `resolved_by`/`marked_spam_at` stamps, one batch audit row), read-marker, hard delete (messages cascade; org-level holds block — `conversation` added to the 0.5 hold-target vocabulary). Routes `/api/app/conversations` (list/counts/detail/patch/read/messages/assign/assign-team/bulk/:verb/delete). Integration: full journey incl. the member-hidden→assigned-visible flip, both bells, note-vs-customer unread semantics, stamps, cascade. inc 52 (Tier B, sync/ingest): the ENTIRE 0.4 mailbox sync + ingest tree REUSED WHOLE (`sync_mailbox.ts` orchestration incl. per-credential watermarks read from NORMALIZED bodies, `ingest/*` — Message-ID idempotent update-in-place, In-Reply-To/References threading, contact find-or-create, attachment reuse-then-materialize) on `domains/conversations/shim.ts`: every internal ref answered from the 0.5 services with rows translated to the 0.4 WIRE SHAPE (`_id`/`_creationTime`, absent-not-null), the mail fetches recursing back into the connector door (injected callback — the domains stay acyclic). Attachment plumbing: `putOrgBlobBytes` + `registerUploadedBytes` (files) + migration 0037's `conversation_id`/`mail_received_at_ms` on file rows (the 0.4 conversation-scope RAG upgrade rides the conversation-corpus retrieval leg — honest-empty until the bind lane queued `rag.index_file` inside the binding transaction and `retrievable.ts` gained its conversation branch; an emailed attachment is now indexed in its conversation's scope). Integration: two-mailbox sync (contacts created, watermark advanced), idempotent re-sync (processed counts the in-place updates — 0.4 semantics — with row counts unchanged), a reply threading into its conversation, and outbound `imap-smtp.send` through the door on a fake SMTP. inc 53 (Tier B, outbound send): the SEND SURFACE — `domains/conversations/send.ts` twins the 0.4 send lane with the PURE pieces REUSED (`attachments` caps, `build_threading_headers`, `reply_from`, `buildReplySubject`/`splitHtmlText`, `connector_slug`, and the NEW `send_input.ts` — `buildSendInput`/`externalIdFromSendOutput` HOISTED out of `internal_actions.ts` into a pure module both stacks import): every path funnels through `sendMessageViaConnector` (queued row with the undo stamps, threading from the latest message, the OLDEST pending `conversations` approval completed on send with the sent-payload fold, monotonic `lastMessageAt`, audit + hint), which schedules `conversation.send_message` (retryLimit 0) one undo window out — the JOB CLAIMS the row with one conditional update (`queued` + unclaimed → `metadata.sendClaimedAt`; a fired job after an undo has nothing to claim and no-ops, an undo after the claim is refused, and the undo's own DELETE re-checks the same predicate: stronger than the 0.4 scheduler-cancel under at-least-once delivery), sends through the connector door as the audited system caller, and settles `sent` + the normalized provider Message-ID or `failed` + `error`/`errorCode` (hint either way). `undoSendMessage` (queued-only, hands `sourceMarkdown` back), `retrySendMessage` (failed-only: job args rebuilt from the row metadata — connector fallback, replyFrom re-resolved, error/undo stamps cleared — immediate, no window), `discardOutboundMessage`, `replyToConversation` (contact-email + connector guards) + `bulkReplyToConversations` (cap 50, sequential partial-failure), `composeEmailConversation` (contact-only, subject required, chosenFrom → `metadata.to`, caps refused BEFORE the conversation exists — the 0.4 atomicity). Routes `POST /:id/reply`, `/compose`, `/bulk/reply` (registered BEFORE `/:id/reply` — Hono's fallback router matches in source order, so the param route would swallow it), `/messages/:messageId/{undo,retry,discard}`. `addJobInTx` now returns the pg-boss job id (stamped as `scheduledSendId` for metadata parity); the undo window is env-tunable (`CONVERSATION_UNDO_SEND_DELAY_MS`, harness 1.5s). Integration: reply → queued (undo stamps + approval completed by the sender) → the delayed job delivers on a fake SMTP (threading + normalized Message-ID asserted), forced failure → `failed`+error → retry re-delivers (retryCount 1), undo returns the draft + the fired job no-ops on the gone row, discard clears a failed bubble, compose opens the outbound conversation, bulk reply 1-of-2 partial failure, send queue drains. inc 56 (Tier B, chat search leg): `domains/conversations/search-chat.ts` twins `search_for_chat.ts` with the same discipline — the Tier-A role gate is nowhere near sufficient, so EVERY row passes the REUSED `conversationAssignmentAllows` predicate (role/team resolved from the caller's identity, never accepted as arguments); the same caps (300-conversation walk, 400-message body pre-pass returning ids only, 25-contact and 50-body match sets) and the same truncation contract (a limit-break is a full answer; a cap-cut names itself); contact matching via the REUSED `rowMatches` + `contactsSearchStrategy`, HTML stripped before body matching. The chat shim's `searchConversationsForChat` honest-empty replaced with the real leg. Integration: subject/body/contact matches for the admin, the member sees exactly their assigned row, a stranger sees nothing. inc 57 (Tier B, address routing): `domains/conversations/routing.ts` twins `address_routing.ts` — the governance hook run INLINE at inbound creation (inside the shim's `createConversationWithMessage`, before downstream notifications observe the row): the org's `conversation_routing` policy FILE (read via `readGovernancePolicyForOrg`; the 0.4 configCache read dies per rule 5) maps the address the customer wrote to (`inboundRecipientAddress`, case-insensitive exact) onto a team queue and/or person; `applyConversationAssignment` validates org membership/team ownership, patches only changed dimensions, audits `assign_conversation` as `system`, and notifies impersonally through the EXISTING collab emitters; an explicit `enabled: false` silences configured rules, and a STALE rule (deleted user/team) warns and leaves the row unassigned — ingest never breaks. Integration: team + person routing (case-insensitive), unknown address, stale rule, kill switch, both bells + both system audit rows. inc 124 closes the row: the scheduled sync packs DO land via provisioning — `seedDefaultAutomationPacks` is the 0.4 `seedDefaultPacks` semantics on the 0.5 store (org-scope packs only, hidden ones skipped, a deliberate deletion's tombstone NOT resurrected, the shipped presentation half refreshed without touching behaviour), and the integration probe watches the real `imap-smtp/sync-emails` pack land at v1 with its trigger and stay at one row on a re-run. The deploy gate stays HUMAN, which is the 0.4 posture: seeding installs the pack, an admin deploys it. The Inbox's own frontend cut over in inc 122                                            