./services/platform/backend/MIGRATION.md:125:| documents             | done                               | inc 10 (Tier A): create-from-upload bind, hub/project scoped reads (access module semantics mirrored), rename/move/team edits, trash/restore, project attach/detach (closes the projects gap), mention search, presigned serve. Tier B landed piecewise: RAG dispatch (knowledge), WebDAV resolvers (inc 61-62), sync configs + hard delete via retention `purgeDocument` (inc 65 — trash stops a directly-selected OneDrive single-file sync, `DocumentRow.historyFiles` exposed, and `purgeDocument` now reaps historyFiles blobs, passed by the retention/erasure/REST callers; pre-65 the replaced-blob history leaked on hard delete). Remaining: controlled records (approvals), replacement uploads (redesign), generate-document lanes. inc 84: the DOCUMENTS VERTICAL part 1 — the Knowledge Hub + project Files tab swapped onto pg end-to-end. Backend: `DocumentRow` grew the shipped-but-unselected 0011 columns (record/scanned_pages_detected/ocr_applied/source_*_at_ms); NEW `domains/documents/view.ts` — the server-side 0.4 `DocumentItemResponse` view (`toDocumentItems`: batch creator/reviewer names, RAG projection joined from `app.file_metadata` by storage_ref, ONE presigned GET per distinct blob via `getFileUrl`, metadata fallbacks incl. sync→auto sourceMode, the controlled-record badge; carries `fileId` extra so the Files-tab light row needs no second endpoint) — `GET /documents[, /by-project/:id, /:id]` now answer ITEM views; `GET /documents/paginated` (keyset (created_at_ms,id) DESC base64url cursor, folder/sourceProvider/extension facets, cap 100), `/approx-count`, `/upload-usage` (`upload_policy.maxTotalVolumeBytesPerUser` over SUM(file_metadata.size)), `/versions/:id` (current + historyFiles decorated from file_metadata; null fail-closed), `/by-external-item-id`, `/search-hub` (title ILIKE over hub-access OR readable projects; 0.4 snippet = folderPath/'Project file'/''), `POST /:id/retry-rag` (the {success,error?} wire: rate-limit + unsupported-terminal + 35-min in-flight guards, then markRagQueued+job), `POST /:id/delete` = HARD delete (project-edit gate, `assertRecordTrashableJson` port, `assertNotHeld`, sync stop, audit, retention `purgeDocument`), `POST /from-blob-upload` = the session bind (statOrgBlob HEAD-attests → `validateDocumentUploadForOrg` — the FULL `checkUploadPolicy` port: extension block/allow, MIME patterns, per-MIME size overrides longest-prefix, volume quota, global allowlist, org rate limit; refusals carry `{code,message,data:{reasonCode,limitBytes,usedBytes}}` via DocumentError.data → registerUploadedBytes → createDocumentFromUpload, one tx so refusals strand nothing), updateDocument grew `teamIds` (0.4 rules: project-doc conflict, folder-inherited team, member-of-team; scope change re-stamps the corpus row via NEW `knowledge.syncRagDocumentScope` — scope-only, no re-embed, best-effort by contract), createDocumentFromUpload grew contentHash + sticky skipRagIndexing. FILES: `POST /files/blob-upload` (size-free presign = the 0.4 generateBlobUpload {url,method:'PUT',s3Ref} wire), `POST /files/upload` (the legacy Convex-POST lane: body → {storageId} where the id IS the org blob ref — every POST-lane uploader works without component surgery; caught live in the browser when the Files tab died on `generateUploadUrl`), `POST /files/reject-blob` (orphan reclaim; bound refs refuse), `statOrgBlob`. FOLDERS: `GET /folders/:id` (null-on-denied view), `POST /folders/:id/teams` (`updateFolderTeams` — 0.4 rules + ONE recursive-CTE cascade re-teaming descendant folders AND documents, touched file-backed docs corpus-restamped post-commit), hub `GET /folders` rows decorated with active sync-config ids (path-keyed, both providers), DELETE became the 0.4 CASCADE (hold + protected-record pre-walks refuse all-or-nothing, sync deactivation, per-doc `purgeDocument`, subtree last; `deleteFolderCascade` lives in documents/service composing cross-dom